{
  "uid": "kafka-lab-payments",
  "title": "Payments — outbox, consumer, API",
  "description": "The four questions an operator asks during an incident, in the order they ask them: is anything piling up, is anything moving, is anything being thrown away, and is the front door still answering.",
  "tags": [
    "kafka-lab"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "5s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-15m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 100,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Is anything running? — read this row before any graph below",
      "description": "Every zero on this dashboard means one of two things: nothing happened, or nothing is left to report it. This row is what tells them apart. Brokers below 3 while the panels below stay green is the shape of a cluster that has lost the quorum that would update them — exp-13 read 0 under-replicated through an outage in which nothing could be published.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": {
                  "text": "DOWN",
                  "color": "red"
                },
                "1": {
                  "text": "up",
                  "color": "green"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byFrameRefID",
              "options": "C"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "mappings",
                "value": []
              },
              {
                "id": "thresholds",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "absolute",
                  "steps": [
                    {
                      "color": "red",
                      "value": null
                    },
                    {
                      "color": "green",
                      "value": 3
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value_and_name"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "up{job=\"payments\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{service}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "expr": "up{job=\"kafka\"}",
          "legendFormat": "kafka-exporter",
          "refId": "B",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "expr": "kafka_brokers",
          "legendFormat": "brokers in the cluster",
          "refId": "C",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Outbox backlog — records waiting to be published",
      "description": "The first number to look at when Kafka is unwell. It grows while nothing can be published, which is the outbox doing its job, and falls once the relay drains. A flat non-zero line means the relay is not running at all.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(outbox_backlog_records{service=\"outbox-relay\"})",
          "legendFormat": "waiting",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Outbox sweeps per second, by outcome",
      "description": "A failing sweep is still a sweep: if this drops to nothing rather than turning red, the relay is gone, not blocked.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (rate(outbox_sweeps_total[30s]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Records published per second",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(outbox_records_published_total{service=\"outbox-relay\"}[30s]))",
          "legendFormat": "published",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Events handled per second — counted against duplicate",
      "description": "Duplicates are at-least-once delivery working. A burst of them after a restart is healthy; a steady stream of them is a relay republishing something it cannot mark.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 13
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (rate(payment_events_handled_total[30s]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Consumer group lag",
      "description": "Read from the cluster, not from the consumer: a consumer that has stopped cannot report its own lag, and that is the moment the number matters.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 21
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "kafka_consumergroup_lag{consumergroup=\"payments-consumer\", topic=\"payments.main\"}",
          "legendFormat": "p{{partition}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Dead letters per second, by reason",
      "description": "Anything here is a record no retry will fix. Undecodable means bytes nobody can read; refused means the consumer understood it and will not take it.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 21
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (reason) (rate(payment_events_dead_lettered_total[30s]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{reason}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "API requests per second, by status",
      "description": "The question this answers during a broker outage: is the front door still taking payments while the events pile up behind it.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 29
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (status) (rate(http_requests_total[30s]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{status}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Under-replicated partitions",
      "description": "Non-zero means a broker is missing from an ISR somewhere. With min.insync.replicas=2 the writes keep going until the second replica goes too.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 29
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (topic) (kafka_topic_partition_under_replicated_partition{topic=~\"payments.*\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{topic}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "API latency, 95th percentile",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 37
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, route) (rate(http_request_duration_seconds_bucket[30s])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{route}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 101,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "The cluster is lying — a backlog piling up while it reports itself healthy",
      "description": "Non-empty means the relay cannot publish while the cluster reports zero under-replicated partitions for payments. That combination is the signature of a lost controller quorum: with no controller nothing updates the metadata the health panels read, so they keep showing the last value they had. exp-13 produced exactly this, and the runbook says to trust the backlog over the cluster's own account of itself.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 45
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 10
          },
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "(sum(outbox_backlog_records{service=\"outbox-relay\"}) > 100) and on() (sum(kafka_topic_partition_under_replicated_partition{topic=~\"payments.*\"}) == 0)",
          "legendFormat": "backlog, with the cluster claiming health",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 102,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Consumer group — members, and offsets going backwards",
      "description": "A dip in members is a rebalance (exp-14) or a member the coordinator dropped (exp-16). A negative bar is a committed offset moving backwards, which is a stale commit rewinding the group — the failure exp-16 proved the lag graph cannot show, because lag was the same whichever handler ran.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 45
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 10
          },
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "kafka_consumergroup_members{consumergroup=\"payments-consumer\"} or min by (topic, partition) (delta(kafka_consumergroup_current_offset{consumergroup=\"payments-consumer\"}[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{__name__}}{{partition}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 103,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Where the consumer is failing, by stage",
      "description": "Without this the only sign of a failing consumer is the handled counter going quiet, which is what an idle one looks like too. exp-11 crash-looped 124–125 times in 30 s and left no mark anywhere. The stage says where to look: fetch is the broker, handle is the database or the domain, commit is the group, dead_letter is the DLQ topic itself — and that last one moving means the offset is not advancing.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 53
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 10
          },
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (stage) (rate(payment_events_failed_total[30s]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{stage}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 104,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "How long the work takes — sweep and event handling, 95th percentile",
      "description": "Both are collected on every sweep and every event and were graphed nowhere. The sweep one matters because the relay's sweep has a fence on it: a p95 climbing toward it is the warning before sweeps start failing.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 53
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 10
          },
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(outbox_sweep_duration_seconds_bucket[30s])))",
          "legendFormat": "outbox sweep",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(payment_event_handling_duration_seconds_bucket[30s])))",
          "legendFormat": "event handling",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
